Here's the patch for the work that has been taking place on the
makefile-infra-rework branch over the past month. Watch out... it's
long 0-o...

I've tested it fairly thoroughly PRIOR to the collapse, BUT any
additional testing is MORE than welcome XD. I will run integration
tests when I return home tonight / sometime tomorrow (08/19/2009).

====================================================================================================

This patch contains any Makefile rework executed as part of the
charter in the README.mk-devel file, as well as any source file
changes required to simplify the Makefile transition, including any
and all consolidation of sources from multiple locations to a common
source (ipv6 vs tcp_cmds for example). The only exception is perf_lan,
which is still split into 2 sourcefiles due to time constraints, and
will be completely consolidated into one sourcefile in the near
future.

No work was done in the rpc / tirpc Makefiles on purpose, as there
aren't executed as part of the default set anyhow. No changes to
ballista nor the open_posix_testsuite's Makefiles were made, but these
will need to be made in the future.

Any sources pulled in after 07/2009 will need to be rewritten to
conform to the new standard as they aren't included with this patch.

Signed-off-by: Garrett Cooper <yanegomi@gmail.com>

